{"archetypes":[{"name":"bash-state-io","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Shell state-file quoting and fallback logic changed across finalize, restore, and stall recovery paths.","prompt_body":"Inspect shell changes in scripts/implement-finalize.sh, scripts/restore-finalize-state.sh, skills/implement/scripts/stall-recovery-report.sh, and write-final-report.sh for state-file parsing, single-quote unescaping, truthiness, and multiline rejection. Check Bash 3.2 portability and whether values written by Python remain readable by existing shell helpers. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"python-shell-parity","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff expands Python ship/finalize behavior that must remain compatible with existing bash contracts.","prompt_body":"Compare Python changes in python/ship.py, python/finalize.py, python/run_context.py, and related tests against the existing shell lifecycle expectations. Look for mismatches in finalize-state contents, stall tracking propagation, tmpdir cleanup allowlists, exit outcomes, and state-file quoting. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"fd-contract","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"Quiet-mode fd 3 and fd 4 routing is subtle and can break machine-readable ship-driver output.","prompt_body":"Review python/logging_util.py and python/ship.py for quiet_init, contract_stream, breadcrumb emission, and inherited file-descriptor handling. Check that JSON contract output, stderr breadcrumbs, fd duplication, and fallback behavior remain safe when quiet mode is already active or disabled. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"artifact-retention","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The stated plan centers on dynamic Codex artifact retention, but the matcher ordering and exclusions are easy to regress.","prompt_body":"Examine scripts/larch-log.sh plus scripts/test-larch-log-write-round.sh and companion docs for the dynamic Codex artifact retention contract. Verify allow and deny ordering, sidecar coverage, phased naming, and that prompt, vote-prompt, telemetry, and static raw Codex transcripts remain excluded as intended. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"ci-toolchain","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff touches Python version gates, pyright config, shared test helpers, and CI-version documentation.","prompt_body":"Review Python toolchain and test-infrastructure changes including python/pyrightconfig.json, python/conftest.py, python/test_support.py, docs/linting.md, and version-gate handling in python/ship.py. Check whether Python 3.11 and 3.12 behavior, type checking, shared runners, and documented CI expectations stay aligned. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
